IMPORT prelude

-- Foreign Acquisitions and Takeovers Act 1975 (Cth) -- the home buyer: am I a foreign person, must I notify the
-- Treasurer before I buy a home, am I exempt because I hold a permanent visa or buy as joint tenants with my spouse,
-- am I barred from buying an established dwelling, and what can I be made to pay if I get it wrong.
--
-- SEAT: the individual buying an interest in residential land in Australia -- here Priya, a permanent resident
-- buying an apartment as joint tenants with her spouse Daniel, an Australian citizen. Every exported question is
-- phrased as that buyer would ask it. The Treasurer's powers (orders, conditions, decisions) appear only as what may be
-- done to the buyer and by when.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 4 (foreign person, limb (a); residential land; established dwelling; new dwelling; temporary
-- resident; Australian land); s 5 (ordinarily resident: the 200-day test and the time limit on presence); s 12(1)(a),
-- (c) (interest in Australian land); s 14 (joint interests are interests); s 43 (significant action -- land); s 47
-- (notifiable action, the land limb); s 49 and s 45(2) (exemption certificates); s 52(1) (threshold test for land
-- without threshold value); s 77(8)(a) (the 30-day decision period); s 81(1) (compulsory notice); s 82(2) (the wait
-- after notice); s 84(1) (the offence of failing to give notice, its penalty); s 94 (civil penalty for a residential
-- land acquisition without notice or before the end of the wait); s 95(1)-(7) (established dwellings: the one-dwelling
-- limit for temporary residents and the bar on other foreign persons; the civil penalty).
-- Regulations used: Foreign Acquisitions and Takeovers Regulation 2015 s 14 (consideration), s 19 (the number of
-- future dwellings: 10), s 28 (excluded provisions), s 35(1)(a) (citizens not ordinarily resident), s 38(2)(a)-(c)
-- (permanent and special category visa holders) and s 38(3) (joint tenants with a spouse or de facto partner who is a
-- citizen, permanent visa holder or special category visa holder), s 52(1)(a) and (2) (residential land has no
-- threshold value, except mixed commercial land).
--
-- Edition: Foreign Acquisitions and Takeovers Act 1975 (No. 92, 1975), Compilation No. 35, compilation date 5 December
-- 2025 (register id C2025C00672), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A01402.txt. Foreign Acquisitions
-- and Takeovers Regulation 2015 (F2015L01854), Compilation No. 20, compilation date 1 November 2025 (register id
-- F2025C01038), as deposited at ../../../foreign-acquisitions-and-takeovers-regulation-2015/registers/source-bundle/
-- F2015L01854.txt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: corporations, trusts, limited partnerships and foreign governments (limbs (b)-(g) of foreign person);
-- entities, businesses, agricultural land, commercial land and mining tenements; national security actions (ss 55A-55G,
-- 66A); the exemption certificates' own tests (ss 57-63: whether a certificate covers the purchase is a FACT); the
-- other regulation exemptions (devolution, custodians, government vendors, timeshares, retirement villages and student
-- accommodation, s 38(4)-(6) and Division 3 generally); interim orders and extended decision periods (ss 68, 77(2)-(7),
-- 77A); the Treasurer's orders and conditions themselves (Part 3); fees (Part 6 and the Fees Imposition Act); vacancy
-- fees (Part 6A); the Register of Foreign Ownership (Part 7A); the capital gain under s 98 (an INPUT); the value of a
-- penalty unit (set by the Crimes Act 1914, not deposited here, so the s 84 fine is given in penalty units); the
-- reg 52(5) threshold for mixed commercial land (an INPUT). The Australian Government's announced two-year ban on
-- foreign persons buying established dwellings from 1 April 2025 is NOT in the deposited Act or Regulation, which have
-- no such date; it is administered through the Treasurer's discretion and is not encoded.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the seat of the home buyer, with the design defaults
-- ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as
-- advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Foreign Acquisitions and Takeovers Act 1975 -- the home buyer`

§§ `The facts the buyer can state`

-- The visa a non-citizen holds, as the Migration Act 1958 names it (a borrowed term, asked as a fact).
DECLARE `Visa held` IS ONE OF
    `none, as an Australian citizen`
    `a permanent visa`
    `a special category visa`
    `a temporary visa allowing a continuous stay of more than 12 months`
    `a temporary visa allowing a continuous stay of 12 months or less`
    `a bridging visa while my permanent visa application is decided`
    `no visa, as an unlawful non-citizen`

-- One individual who buys, or buys with the buyer.
DECLARE Person HAS
    `is an Australian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `visa` IS A `Visa held`
    `days in Australia in the last 12 months` IS A NUMBER
    `as a citizen, ordinarily resides in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `special category visa leaves the stay limited in time` IS A BOOLEAN
    `would be entitled to a special category visa on presenting a passport` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is residing in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN

-- How the interest is to be held (s 14: a joint interest is still an interest; reg 38(3) turns on "joint tenants").
DECLARE Holding IS ONE OF
    `alone`
    `as joint tenants with my spouse or de facto partner`
    `as tenants in common with my spouse or de facto partner`
    `with someone who is not my spouse or de facto partner`

-- s 12(1): the kind of interest being acquired.
DECLARE `Kind of interest` IS ONE OF
    `a legal or equitable interest such as freehold`
    `a lease or licence reasonably likely to exceed 5 years`
    `a lease or licence not reasonably likely to exceed 5 years`

-- The land and the dwelling being bought.
DECLARE Purchase HAS
    `interest` IS A `Kind of interest`
    `dwellings on the land` IS A NUMBER
    `dwellings that could reasonably be built on the land` IS A NUMBER
    `land is used wholly and exclusively for a primary production business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `only dwellings are commercial residential premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is non-vacant commercial land with a residential part under 10 percent by area and value` IS A BOOLEAN
    `value exceeds the reg 52(5) threshold` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dwelling has been sold as a dwelling before` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dwelling has been occupied before` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dwelling is in a development and sold by its developer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months the dwelling has been occupied in total` IS A NUMBER
    `holding` IS A Holding
    `the co-owner` IS A Person
    `an exemption certificate, no objection notification or notice imposing conditions covers it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `consideration` IS A NUMBER
    `market value of the interest` IS A NUMBER
    `capital gain under s 98` IS A NUMBER
    `other established dwellings I already hold` IS A NUMBER
    `genuinely trying to sell, under 6 months over the limit` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `s 5 -- ordinarily resident`

-- s 5(1): "An individual who is not an Australian citizen is ordinarily resident in Australia at a particular time if
-- and only if: (a) the individual has actually been in Australia during 200 or more days in the period of 12 months
-- immediately preceding that time; and (b) ... the individual's continued presence in Australia is not subject to any
-- limitation as to time imposed by law". (2): an unlawful non-citizen's presence is subject to such a limitation.
-- Gloss: a permanent visa sets no time limit. A temporary or bridging visa runs for a period or until a decision, so
-- the encoding INFERS that it is a time limit. For a special category visa the answer is asked as a fact.
-- s 5(1)(b)(ii) (absent from Australia) asks about the visa held immediately before leaving; the encoding uses the one
-- visa fact for both.
GIVEN `p` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`presence is subject to a time limit imposed by law` MEANS
    CONSIDER `p`'s `visa`
    WHEN `none, as an Australian citizen` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a permanent visa` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a special category visa` THEN `p`'s `special category visa leaves the stay limited in time`
    WHEN `a temporary visa allowing a continuous stay of more than 12 months` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a temporary visa allowing a continuous stay of 12 months or less` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a bridging visa while my permanent visa application is decided` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `no visa, as an unlawful non-citizen` THEN TRUE

-- s 5 speaks only of non-citizens. Whether a citizen is ordinarily resident takes its ordinary meaning, asked as a fact.
@export Am I ordinarily resident in Australia under s 5?
GIVEN `me` IS A Person @desc About you: citizenship, visa, days in Australia
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I ordinarily resident in Australia` IF
    IF `me`'s `is an Australian citizen`
    THEN `me`'s `as a citizen, ordinarily resides in Australia`
    ELSE     `me`'s `days in Australia in the last 12 months` AT LEAST 200
         AND (NOT `presence is subject to a time limit imposed by law` `me`)

§§ `s 4 -- foreign person, temporary resident`

-- s 4: "foreign person means: (a) an individual not ordinarily resident in Australia; ..." Limbs (b)-(g)
-- (corporations, trusts, foreign governments, persons prescribed) are not encoded.
-- Reg 28 note: the regulation exemptions "are taken into account for the purposes of the definition of foreign
-- person": an exempt buyer is still a foreign person; the exemption removes the duty to notify, not the status.
@export Am I a foreign person under s 4?
GIVEN `me` IS A Person @desc About you: citizenship, visa, days in Australia
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a foreign person` IF
    NOT `Am I ordinarily resident in Australia` `me`

-- s 4: "temporary resident means an individual who: (a) holds a temporary visa ... that allows the individual to
-- remain in Australia for a continuous period of more than 12 months ...; or (b) ... is residing in Australia; ... has
-- applied for a permanent visa ...; ... holds a bridging visa ... until the application has been finally determined;
-- or (c) meets the conditions prescribed by the regulations." The Regulation prescribes none.
@export Am I a temporary resident under s 4?
GIVEN `me` IS A Person @desc About you: citizenship, visa, residence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a temporary resident` IF
    CONSIDER `me`'s `visa`
    WHEN `a temporary visa allowing a continuous stay of more than 12 months` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a bridging visa while my permanent visa application is decided` THEN `me`'s `is residing in Australia`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `s 4, s 12 -- the land and the interest`

-- s 4: "residential land: (a) means land in Australia if: (i) there is at least one dwelling on the land; or (ii) the
-- number of dwellings that could reasonably be built on the land is less than the number prescribed by the
-- regulations; and (b) does not include land: (i) used wholly and exclusively for a primary production business; or
-- (ii) on which the only dwellings are commercial residential premises." Reg 19: the number is 10.
`the reg 19 number of future dwellings` MEANS 10

@export Is the land I am buying residential land under s 4?
GIVEN `the purchase` IS A Purchase @desc The land and dwelling you are buying
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it residential land` IF
        (    `the purchase`'s `dwellings on the land` AT LEAST 1
          OR `the purchase`'s `dwellings that could reasonably be built on the land` LESS THAN `the reg 19 number of future dwellings`)
    AND (NOT `the purchase`'s `land is used wholly and exclusively for a primary production business`)
    AND (NOT `the purchase`'s `only dwellings are commercial residential premises`)

-- s 12(1)(a): "a legal or equitable interest in Australian land, other than: (i) an interest under a lease or licence";
-- (c): a lease or licence "if the term ... is reasonably likely ... to exceed 5 years". s 4: Australian land includes
-- residential land.
@export Am I acquiring an interest in Australian land under s 12?
GIVEN `the purchase` IS A Purchase @desc The land and dwelling you are buying
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I acquiring an interest in Australian land` IF
        `Is it residential land` `the purchase`
    AND (CONSIDER `the purchase`'s `interest`
         WHEN `a lease or licence not reasonably likely to exceed 5 years` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)

-- s 4: "new dwelling means a dwelling ... that will be, is being or has been built on residential land and that: (a)
-- has not been previously sold as a dwelling; and (b) either: (i) has not been previously occupied; or (ii) if the
-- dwelling is contained in a development and the dwelling was sold by the developer of the development -- has not been
-- previously occupied for more than 12 months in total." "established dwelling means a dwelling ... on residential land
-- that is not a new dwelling."
GIVEN `the purchase` IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a new dwelling` MEANS
        `Is it residential land` `the purchase`
    AND (NOT `the purchase`'s `dwelling has been sold as a dwelling before`)
    AND (    (NOT `the purchase`'s `dwelling has been occupied before`)
          OR (     `the purchase`'s `dwelling is in a development and sold by its developer`
               AND `the purchase`'s `months the dwelling has been occupied in total` AT MOST 12))

@export Is the home I am buying an established dwelling under s 4?
GIVEN `the purchase` IS A Purchase @desc The land and dwelling you are buying
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it an established dwelling` IF
        `Is it residential land` `the purchase`
    AND `the purchase`'s `dwellings on the land` AT LEAST 1
    AND (NOT `is a new dwelling` `the purchase`)

§§ `s 52 and reg 52 -- the threshold test`

-- s 52(1): "The threshold test is met in relation to land if the land is of a kind that is prescribed by the
-- regulations for the purposes of this subsection." Reg 52(1)(a): "residential land, except residential land covered
-- by subsection (2)". Reg 52(2): land that is also non-vacant commercial land whose residential part is under 10% of
-- its area and value; its threshold (reg 52(5) table) is an INPUT.
@export Is the threshold test met for the land I am buying (s 52)?
GIVEN `the purchase` IS A Purchase @desc The land and dwelling you are buying
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the threshold test met` IF
        `Is it residential land` `the purchase`
    AND (    (NOT `the purchase`'s `is non-vacant commercial land with a residential part under 10 percent by area and value`)
          OR `the purchase`'s `value exceeds the reg 52(5) threshold`)

§§ `Regulation Part 3 Division 3 -- the exemptions for home buyers`

-- Reg 28: the exempting provisions switch off the "excluded provisions" (the whole Act except the definition of
-- foreign person), so an exempt acquisition is not a significant action or notifiable action.
DECLARE Exemption IS ONE OF
    `no exemption applies`
    `reg 35(1)(a): an Australian citizen not ordinarily resident in Australia`
    `reg 38(2)(a): the holder of a permanent visa`
    `reg 38(2)(b): the holder of a special category visa`
    `reg 38(2)(c): entitled to a special category visa on presenting a passport`
    `reg 38(3): joint tenants with a spouse or partner who is a citizen or holds a permanent or special category visa`

-- Reg 38(3)(a): the spouse or de facto partner is "(i) ... an Australian citizen; or (ii) ... the holder of a permanent
-- visa ...; or (iii) ... the holder of a special category visa ...; or (iv) a person who ... would have been entitled to
-- the grant ... of a special category visa".
GIVEN `p` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a qualifying spouse under reg 38(3)(a)` MEANS
       `p`'s `is an Australian citizen`
    OR `holds a permanent visa` `p`
    OR `holds a special category visa` `p`
    OR `p`'s `would be entitled to a special category visa on presenting a passport`

GIVEN `p` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`holds a permanent visa` MEANS
    CONSIDER `p`'s `visa`
    WHEN `a permanent visa` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `p` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`holds a special category visa` MEANS
    CONSIDER `p`'s `visa`
    WHEN `a special category visa` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the purchase` IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is held as joint tenants with my spouse` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the purchase`'s `holding`
    WHEN `as joint tenants with my spouse or de facto partner` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The first exemption that applies, in the order of the Regulation.
@export Which exemption in the Regulation applies to my purchase of residential land?
GIVEN `me` IS A Person @desc About you: citizenship, visa, days in Australia
      `the purchase` IS A Purchase @desc The land and dwelling you are buying, and with whom
GIVETH AN Exemption
DECIDE `Which exemption applies to me` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `me`'s `is an Australian citizen` AND `Am I a foreign person` `me`
            THEN `reg 35(1)(a): an Australian citizen not ordinarily resident in Australia`
        IF (NOT `Is it residential land` `the purchase`)
            THEN `no exemption applies`
        IF `holds a permanent visa` `me`
            THEN `reg 38(2)(a): the holder of a permanent visa`
        IF `holds a special category visa` `me`
            THEN `reg 38(2)(b): the holder of a special category visa`
        IF `me`'s `would be entitled to a special category visa on presenting a passport`
            THEN `reg 38(2)(c): entitled to a special category visa on presenting a passport`
        IF     `is held as joint tenants with my spouse` `the purchase`
           AND `is a qualifying spouse under reg 38(3)(a)` (`the purchase`'s `the co-owner`)
            THEN `reg 38(3): joint tenants with a spouse or partner who is a citizen or holds a permanent or special category visa`
        OTHERWISE `no exemption applies`

GIVEN `me` IS A Person
      `the purchase` IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an exemption applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Which exemption applies to me` `me` `the purchase`
    WHEN `no exemption applies` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `s 47, s 49 -- is my purchase a notifiable action`

-- s 47(2)(c): "to acquire an interest in Australian land"; (3): "the threshold test is met"; (5): "the action is or is
-- to be taken by a foreign person". s 49(1) with s 45(2): not notifiable if an exemption certificate covering the
-- interest is in force and its conditions are met (a FACT here). Reg 28: not notifiable if a regulation exemption
-- applies.
@export Is my purchase a notifiable action under s 47?
GIVEN `me` IS A Person @desc About you: citizenship, visa, days in Australia
      `the purchase` IS A Purchase @desc The land and dwelling you are buying, and with whom
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my purchase a notifiable action` IF
        `Am I acquiring an interest in Australian land` `the purchase`
    AND `Is the threshold test met` `the purchase`
    AND `Am I a foreign person` `me`
    AND (NOT `an exemption applies` `me` `the purchase`)
    AND (NOT `the purchase`'s `an exemption certificate, no objection notification or notice imposing conditions covers it`)

§§ `s 81, s 82, s 77 -- notice, and the wait`

-- s 81(1): "A foreign person who proposes to take a notifiable action ... must give a notice to the Treasurer before
-- taking the action." s 15(4)-(5) (note to s 81): an action taken by entering an agreement is not taken until the
-- agreement is binding.
@export Must I notify the Treasurer before I buy (s 81)?
GIVEN `me` IS A Person @desc About you: citizenship, visa, days in Australia
      `the purchase` IS A Purchase @desc The land and dwelling you are buying, and with whom
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I notify the Treasurer before I buy` IF
    `Is my purchase a notifiable action` `me` `the purchase`

-- s 77(8)(a): a decision period is "the period of 30 days after the day" the Treasurer receives the notice.
-- s 82(2): the foreign person "must not take the action before the earliest of ... (a) the day that is 10 days after the
-- end of the decision period ...; (b) if an interim order is made -- the end of the period specified in the order; (c)
-- the day a no objection notification is given to the person." Interim orders, extensions and the s 77(7) pause for a
-- s 133 notice are not encoded; s 114 (notice not given until the fee is paid) is not encoded either.
`the decision period in days` MEANS 30
`days after the decision period ends` MEANS 10

@export If I give notice, how many days after the Treasurer receives it must I wait before buying (s 82)?
GIVEN `no objection notification received` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Treasurer has given you a no objection notification
      `its day after receipt of my notice` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many days after receiving your notice the Treasurer gave it
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days must I wait before buying` IS
    IF     `no objection notification received`
       AND `its day after receipt of my notice` LESS THAN (`the decision period in days` PLUS `days after the decision period ends`)
    THEN `its day after receipt of my notice`
    ELSE `the decision period in days` PLUS `days after the decision period ends`

§§ `s 95 -- established dwellings`

-- s 95(4): "A foreign person who is not a temporary resident must not acquire an interest in an established dwelling."
-- s 95(5): not if the interest is specified in "(a) an exemption certificate; or (b) a no objection notification; or
-- (c) a notice imposing conditions". Reg 28: the regulation exemptions switch s 95 off too.
@export Am I barred from buying this established dwelling (s 95(4))?
GIVEN `me` IS A Person @desc About you: citizenship, visa, days in Australia
      `the purchase` IS A Purchase @desc The land and dwelling you are buying, and with whom
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I barred from buying this established dwelling` IF
        `Am I a foreign person` `me`
    AND (NOT `Am I a temporary resident` `me`)
    AND `Is it an established dwelling` `the purchase`
    AND `Am I acquiring an interest in Australian land` `the purchase`
    AND (NOT `an exemption applies` `me` `the purchase`)
    AND (NOT `the purchase`'s `an exemption certificate, no objection notification or notice imposing conditions covers it`)

-- s 95(1): "A foreign person who is a temporary resident must not hold an interest in more than one established
-- dwelling at the same time." (2): not while "(a) ... making a genuine attempt to dispose of one or more of the
-- interests; and (b) if those interests were disposed of, the person would not contravene subsection (1); and (c) the
-- person has been holding an interest in more than one established dwelling for less than 6 months." (3)(a): not for a
-- dwelling that was new when acquired (an established dwelling being bought now is not).
@export Would buying this established dwelling put me over the one-dwelling limit for temporary residents (s 95(1))?
GIVEN `me` IS A Person @desc About you: citizenship, visa, residence
      `the purchase` IS A Purchase @desc The land and dwelling you are buying, and what you already hold
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Would I break the one established dwelling limit` IF
        `Am I a foreign person` `me`
    AND `Am I a temporary resident` `me`
    AND `Is it an established dwelling` `the purchase`
    AND `the purchase`'s `other established dwellings I already hold` AT LEAST 1
    AND (NOT `the purchase`'s `genuinely trying to sell, under 6 months over the limit`)
    AND (NOT `an exemption applies` `me` `the purchase`)
    AND (NOT `the purchase`'s `an exemption certificate, no objection notification or notice imposing conditions covers it`)

§§ `ss 84, 94, 95(7) -- what I can be made to pay`

-- s 94(4) and s 95(7): "the greatest of the following: (a) double the amount of the capital gain that was made or would
-- be made on the disposal of the interest ...; (b) 50% of the consideration for the ... acquisition; (c) 50% of the
-- market value of the interest". The capital gain (s 98) is an INPUT. Reg 14: consideration "includes ... consideration
-- in any form" and GST.
GIVEN `the purchase` IS A Purchase
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the residential land penalty ceiling` MEANS
    `the greater of`
        (2 TIMES `the purchase`'s `capital gain under s 98`)
        (`the greater of`
            (`the purchase`'s `consideration` DIVIDED BY 2)
            (`the purchase`'s `market value of the interest` DIVIDED BY 2))

-- s 94(1): a foreign person who proposes a notifiable residential land acquisition "must not take the action if the
-- foreign person has not given a notice"; (3): civil penalty. Zero where no notice was required.
@export If I buy without notifying, what is the most civil penalty I can be ordered to pay (s 94)?
GIVEN `me` IS A Person @desc About you: citizenship, visa, days in Australia
      `the purchase` IS A Purchase @desc The land and dwelling you are buying, its price and value
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be made to pay for buying without notice` IS
    IF `Must I notify the Treasurer before I buy` `me` `the purchase`
    THEN `the residential land penalty ceiling` `the purchase`
    ELSE 0

@export If I buy an established dwelling I am barred from, what is the most civil penalty I can be ordered to pay (s 95(7))?
GIVEN `me` IS A Person @desc About you: citizenship, visa, days in Australia
      `the purchase` IS A Purchase @desc The land and dwelling you are buying, its price and value
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be made to pay for an established dwelling` IS
    IF     `Am I barred from buying this established dwelling` `me` `the purchase`
        OR `Would I break the one established dwelling limit` `me` `the purchase`
    THEN `the residential land penalty ceiling` `the purchase`
    ELSE 0

-- s 84(1): a foreign person who takes a notifiable action without a notice under s 81(1) commits an offence. "Penalty:
-- Imprisonment for 10 years, or 15,000 penalty units ..., or both." s 90 keeps the general civil penalties (ss 91-93)
-- off residential land, but nothing in Division 2 keeps s 84 off it.
@export If I must notify and do not, what is the longest prison term for the offence (s 84), in years?
GIVEN `me` IS A Person @desc About you: citizenship, visa, days in Australia
      `the purchase` IS A Purchase @desc The land and dwelling you are buying, and with whom
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest prison term for not notifying in years` IS
    IF `Must I notify the Treasurer before I buy` `me` `the purchase` THEN 10 ELSE 0

@export If I must notify and do not, what is the largest fine for the offence (s 84), in penalty units?
GIVEN `me` IS A Person @desc About you: citizenship, visa, days in Australia
      `the purchase` IS A Purchase @desc The land and dwelling you are buying, and with whom
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the largest fine for not notifying in penalty units` IS
    IF `Must I notify the Treasurer before I buy` `me` `the purchase` THEN 15000 ELSE 0
